    "type": "question",
    "label": "19",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following. $\\dfrac{y^2}{y^5}$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y^{-3}=\\dfrac1{y^3}$, $y\\ne0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{y^2}{y^5}&=y^{2-5}\\\\\\frac{y^2}{y^5}&=y^{-3}\\\\\\frac{y^2}{y^5}&=\\frac1{y^3}\\end{align*}$$The original denominator requires $y\\ne0$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
